---

This module vendors no third-party source and has zero runtime
dependencies: it consumes only the Go standard library (BSD-3-Clause),
including the crypto/ed25519 and crypto/sha256 packages. The vendored
conformance corpus snapshot under conformance/corpus/ is protocol test
data authored in this repository.

---

Third-party test vectors

The strict-Ed25519 conformance snapshot file
conformance/corpus-strict/cases/taming/speccheck.json contains 12 Ed25519 test vectors
imported byte for byte from ed25519-speccheck
(https://github.com/novifinancial/ed25519-speccheck, commit
65519336fda78a3d016e947df6d82848aca0c9da, file cases.json, SHA-256
08e47a36d9aead288664930505584f353fff113ab854f2800db1e4f5b3540450), which
accompanies "Taming the many EdDSAs" (Chalkias, Garillot, Nikolaenko,
SSR 2020; IACR ePrint 2020/1244). Copyright (c) Facebook, Inc. and its
affiliates. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; the upstream
repository carries no NOTICE file at that commit. The vectors are reproduced
unmodified; the snapshot adds the base64url input encoding, expected verdicts,
and provenance fields around them. The snapshot is a byte-identical copy of
the repository's priv/conformance/strict-ed25519/ corpus.
